-- title:
--   Local n-th roots near a scalar in a regular semisimple centraliser
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $v$ be a nonzero prime ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$ (a point of `HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)`), and write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion `v.adicCompletion K`. Let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ be such that $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit of $K_v$, which is the content of [`AutomorphicForm.IsRegularSemisimple`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L402) for the matrix underlying $\gamma_0$; let $c \in K_v^{\times}$ and let $n$ be a natural number with $n > 0$. The assertion is that for every neighbourhood $V'$ of the identity in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ there is a neighbourhood $W$ of the scalar matrix $c \cdot 1_2$, given by `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.scalar (Fin 2) c`, such that every $\gamma \in W$ lying in [`AutomorphicForm.localCentralizer K v γ₀`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L193), i.e. in the centraliser of the singleton $\{\gamma_0\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, admits an element $\beta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ with three properties: $\beta$ lies in $V'$; the matrix underlying $\beta$ lies in the $K_v$-subalgebra `Algebra.adjoin` of $M_2(K_v)$ generated by the matrix underlying $\gamma_0$; and $\beta^n = (c\cdot 1_2)^{-1}\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$.
--
--   This is the statement that in the maximal torus $Z_{\mathrm{GL}_2}(\gamma_0)(K_v) \subseteq K_v[\gamma_0]^{\times}$ attached to a regular semisimple element over a nonarchimedean local field, elements sufficiently close to the central point $c \cdot 1_2$ are $c$ times an $n$-th power of a torus element arbitrarily close to $1$. It is used in the local analysis of twisted weighted orbital integrals, in particular by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_exists_isTwistedWeightedOrbitalIntegral_of_normString_eq_toTensorGL_scalar_mul_diagUnits2`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_exists_isTwistedWeightedOrbitalIntegral_of_normString_eq_toTensorGL_scalar_mul_diagUnits2) and by the construction of norm conjugators in [`AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_mem_localCentralizer_isNormConjugator_mul_of_isNormConjugator_mul`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_mem_localCentralizer_isNormConjugator_mul_of_isNormConjugator_mul).
